meta {
  name: Approve Write Request
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/write-requests/{{writeRequestId}}/approve
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "notes": "Looks correct — approved."
  }
}

docs {
  Approve and execute a PENDING request. Requires approve capability for the env; you cannot approve your own.

  409 if the request's connection was edited (env, type, host, port, database, username, default schema, URI), or deleted and re-created, since the request was submitted — "Connection <id> changed since this request was submitted — re-approve it…" — or no longer exists. Nothing runs and the request stays PENDING; cancel or reject it and resubmit (revise) to bind it to the current connection. Renaming the connection or rotating its password does not trigger this.

  503 `CONNECTION_FAILED` when the database can't be reached before anything is sent: nothing ran, the request stays PENDING, and the body carries it as `request`. Audited as `WRITE_EXECUTE_ERROR`.

  Requires a valid Bearer JWT ({{token}}).
  Requires **write mode** to be enabled.
}
